{"name":"Jazz","hex":"#5f2c2f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jazz","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A diminutive of the male given name Jasper.","A diminutive of the male given name James."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jazz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jazz","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz is a music genre that originated in the African-American communities of New Orleans, Louisiana, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Its roots are in blues, ragtime, European harmony, African rhythmic rituals, spirituals, hymns, marches, vaudeville song, and dance music. Since the 1920s Jazz Age, it has been recognized as a major form of musical expression in both traditional and popular music. Jazz is characterized by swing and blue notes, complex chords, call and response vocals, polyrhythms and improvisation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz","wikidata":"Q8341"},{"title":"Jazz (Queen album)","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz is the seventh studio album by the British rock band Queen. It was co-produced by Roy Thomas Baker, and was released on 10 November 1978 by EMI Records in the United Kingdom and by Elektra Records in the United States. The album artwork was suggested by Roger Taylor, who had seen a similar design painted on the Berlin Wall. The album's varying musical styles were alternately praised and criticised. It reached number two in the UK Albums Chart and number six on the US Billboard Top LPs & Tape chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Queen_Jazz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz_(Queen_album)","wikidata":"Q270083"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Ford Madox Brown - The Last of England - Google Art Project","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_